        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "## Done — a real INI parser for this repo's dialect\n\n`moon test` → **62/62 pass** (12 public + 50 of mine). `moon check` reports **0 errors and 0 diagnostics from any file I wrote**; all 6 remaining warnings are pre-existing ones inside the protected files.\n\n### Implementation (root `ini` package, 8 focused modules, 60–150 lines each)\n\n| file | role |\n| --- | --- |\n| [region.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\region.mbt) | `Region` — a `[start,end)` window into one shared `Array[Char]`; trimming; blank / control-char / comment-marker classes |\n| [lines.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\lines.mbt) | LF/CRLF line splitting |\n| [escape.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\escape.mbt) | `Carrier` (unquoted / `\"…\"` / `'…'`) and its per-carrier escape table |\n| [value.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\value.mbt) | quoted values, unquoted values with comment stripping + backslash continuation |\n| [section.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\section.mbt) | header parsing: trim, strip one wrapping quote pair, reject brackets/empties/trailing text |\n| [entry.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\entry.mbt) | first `=`/`:` separator, key validation, dispatch to the value parsers |\n| [parse.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\parse.mbt) | line classification + document assembly (global map, section re-open via map aliasing, last-wins) |\n| [print.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\print.mbt) | normalising printer: `key = \"value\"`, section names wrapped only when needed |\n\nKey decisions that follow `specs/ini.md`: continuation is decided on the **raw** trailing-backslash run *before* escapes/comments (odd = marker, even = literals); an inline comment needs a preceding blank and is stripped from the entry's own line only, so a continuation line contributes text (its `=`, `:`, quotes and `;`/`#` are ordinary); quoted values never span lines and reject trailing text; keys are verbatim except for trimming and the control-character ban.\n\n### Verification beyond the public tests\n- [ini_edge_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\ini_edge_test.mbt): 50 spec-derived cases, including the full escape table per carrier, the continuation run-length table (N=1–4), marker-before-CRLF, whitespace-vs-escape trimming, every rejection class, git-config/systemd/php.ini samples, and two deterministic fuzz tests.\n- [dev/main.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\dev\\main.mbt) (`moon run dev`): ~200-case catalogue plus sweeps — 100k random inputs, all inputs to length 5 over an 11-char alphabet, 30k generated documents — all with 0 round-trip problems and no panics. It found one real printer bug (a section name holding both quote kinds plus a trailing blank lost the blank), now pinned by a test.\n- An independent audit (`@builtin/review.mbtx`) reported **0 blockers**; its two documentation nits (state the \"expressible in INI\" qualifier for `print`, and note the Map-aliasing dependency in `parse`) are applied.\n\n### Other notes\n- [README.md](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\README.md) documents overview, architecture, algorithms (with the escape/continuation tables), usage, testing and design rationale.\n- `moon.pkg`: moved `moonbitlang/core/test` to `import … for \"test\"`, which removes the pre-existing `unused_package` warning without changing what test files see.\n- Protected files are **content-identical to the originals** (`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `ini_pub_test.mbt`, `moon.mod`, `specs/ini.md` — verified by diff). `moon fmt` was run, but this toolchain also rewrites those protected files (`derive(…)` → `#derive(…)`, `Int` → `Int32`); I reverted them, so only they still appear in `moon fmt --check`, exactly as before my work. My files are formatter-clean and `moon info` regenerated `pkg.generated.mbti`.\n- `dev/` is a separate executable package kept as a documented self-check tool; the `remove` tool needs an approval channel this session doesn't have, so it could not be deleted — it is documented in the README instead."
        }
