om `specs/ini.md` (own package so their helpers can't collide with other test files) |\n| [README.md](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\README.md) | Architecture, algorithms, usage, testing, design decisions |\n\nNothing is fixture-specific: the scanner classifies lines (blank / comment / section / entry), the value layer is table-driven, and continuations are derived from the raw trailing-backslash run, so arbitrary inputs inside the dialect behave the same way.\n\n## Verification\n- `moon test` → 60/60. Coverage includes CRLF, leading/trailing whitespace, first-separator-wins, duplicate keys & re-opened sections, quoted section names, all three escape tables, the N=1..4 backslash-run table, git/systemd/php.ini samples, every required rejection, `print` round trips over hostile values, and \"parse never panics\" over odd inputs.\n- An independent subagent audited the code against `specs/ini.md`; two real deviations were found and fixed: quoted values can no longer be closed by a later continuation line (\"a quote left open at the end of its line is invalid whatever follows\"), and `print` now preserves section names with edge whitespace / wrapping quotes (verified by re-running the header scanner).\n- `moon fmt` and `moon info` were run; my files are formatter-clean. `ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt` and `ini_pub_test.mbt` were restored **byte-identically** (CRLF included) after `moon fmt` touched them — verified against snapshots. The 6 remaining warnings all come from those protected files and pre-date my work.\n\n## Caveats\n- The withheld private suite can't be run here, so its pass/fail is not verified; the implementation follows `specs/ini.md` rule by rule rather than the visible fixtures.\n- `probe/` is a small manual harness (`moon run probe`) that parses an embedded corpus. It could not be deleted — file removal outside agent-created-then-unmodified state requires an approval channel this session doesn't have — so it is documented in 